---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<SiteLayout title="AgentX — Build with an agent that can see the whole project." description="AgentX is a terminal-first coding agent that understands your repository before changing it.">
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">TERMINAL-FIRST CODING AGENT</p>
        <h1>Build with an agent that can see the whole project.</h1>
        <p>AgentX reads your repository, plans the work, changes the right files, and uses project checks to verify the result.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/docs/installation/">Install AgentX</a>
          <a class="button" href="/docs/intro/">Read the docs</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal">
        <div class="terminal-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <pre><code>$ agentx
Plan → Read → Execute → Verify

> Inspecting repository
> Building an implementation plan
> Ready for your approval</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE CORE IDEA</p>
      <h2>Understand the code before you change the code.</h2>
      <p>AgentX is designed around repository awareness, explicit plans, native terminal workflows, and verification.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
